n","dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Installation","title":"Helper Functions for r-xla","text":"","code":"pak::pak(\"r-xla/xlamisc\")"},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/index.html","id":"available-generics","dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Available Generics","title":"Helper Functions for r-xla","text":"shape(): Different dim() also supporting 0-dimensional tensors. dtype(): Returns data type tensor. as_array(): Converts tensor R array. as_raw(): Converts tensor raw() vector. device(): Returns device tensor. functions: naxes(): Returns number axes tensor. implemented length(shape(x)). nelts(): Returns number elements tensor. implemented prod(shape(x)).","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/index.html","id":"tensor-data-types","dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Tensor Data Types","title":"Helper Functions for r-xla","text":"xlamisc provides DataType, enum-style S3 class representing tensor element type. one singleton object per supported dtype, wrapping canonical string. members : boolean: bool (aliases i1, pred) signed integers: i8, i16, i32, i64 unsigned integers: ui8, ui16, ui32, ui64 floats: f16, bf16, f32, f64 complex: c64, c128 Construct inspect data types : as_dtype(x): Convert string (e.g. \"f32\") DataType DataType object. is_dtype(x): Check whether object DataType. assert_dtype(x): Assert object DataType. dtype_width(x): width one element bits. dtype_category(x): category, one \"bool\", \"int\", \"uint\", \"float\", \"complex\". is_dtype_float(x), is_dtype_int(x), is_dtype_uint(x), is_dtype_bool(x), is_dtype_complex(x): Per-category predicates. Data types support equality comparison == !=.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/DataType.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"DataType — DataType","title":"DataType — DataType","text":"DataType S3 class representing tensor element type. enum: one singleton object per supported dtype, wrapping canonical dtype string. members element types supported r-xla stack: boolean: bool signed integers: i8, i16, i32, i64 unsigned integers: ui8, ui16, ui32, ui64 floats: f16, bf16, f32, f64 complex: c64, c128 Construct DataType as_dtype(). Inspect dtype_width() is_dtype_float() family predicates.","code":""},{"path":[]},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_array.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"As Array — as_array","title":"As Array — as_array","text":"Convert value (usually tensor framework) R array.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_array.html","id":"ref-usage","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Usage","title":"As Array — as_array","text":"","code":"as_array(x, ...)"},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_array.html","id":"arguments","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Arguments","title":"As Array — as_array","text":"x () Object. ... () Additional arguments.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_array.html","id":"value","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Value","title":"As Array — as_array","text":"()","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_dtype.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Convert to DataType — as_dtype","title":"Convert to DataType — as_dtype","text":"Convert DataType.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_dtype.html","id":"ref-usage","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Usage","title":"Convert to DataType — as_dtype","text":"","code":"as_dtype(x)"},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_dtype.html","id":"arguments","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Arguments","title":"Convert to DataType — as_dtype","text":"x () dtype string (e.g. \"f32\", \"i64\", \"bool\"; aliases \"pred\" \"i1\" map \"bool\") DataType object.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_dtype.html","id":"value","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Value","title":"Convert to DataType — as_dtype","text":"DataType","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_raw.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"As Raw — as_raw","title":"As Raw — as_raw","text":"Convert value (usually tensor framework) raw() vector.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_raw.html","id":"ref-usage","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Usage","title":"As Raw — as_raw","text":"","code":"as_raw(x, ...)"},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_raw.html","id":"arguments","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Arguments","title":"As Raw — as_raw","text":"x () Object. ... () Additional arguments.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/as_raw.html","id":"value","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Value","title":"As Raw — as_raw","text":"()","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/assert_dtype.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Assert DataType — assert_dtype","title":"Assert DataType — assert_dtype","text":"Assert object DataType.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/assert_dtype.html","id":"ref-usage","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Usage","title":"Assert DataType — assert_dtype","text":"","code":"assert_dtype(x, arg = rlang::caller_arg(x))"},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/assert_dtype.html","id":"arguments","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Arguments","title":"Assert DataType — assert_dtype","text":"x () Object check. arg (character(1)) Argument name error messages.","code":""},{"path":"https://r-xla.github.io/xlamisc/reference/assert_dtype.html","id":"value","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Value","title":"Assert DataType — assert_dtype","text":"NULL (invisibly). Called side effects.","code":""},{"path":"ht